From e5c99358b785275bb198eecfa1f56f2ca87f8f53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JuggyMcNutty <11588877+JuggyMcNutty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 06:53:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Non-bindless fallback path and texture format support checks

Two changes so the Vulkan renderer survives GPUs without desktop texture
support. Both were tested on a PowerVR Rogue GE8300 (TrimUI Smart Pro,
Vulkan 1.3.225) where the game previously stopped at device selection.

Non-bindless texture path (SURREAL_VK_NO_BINDLESS=1 forces it on capable
GPUs for testing):

- The device no longer requires VK_EXT_descriptor_indexing outright; the
  renderer falls back to one four-binding descriptor set per texture
  combination when descriptor indexing is missing.
- DescriptorSetManager grows SceneLayout/SceneSets/SceneSetCache with
  pooled allocation; VulkanRenderDevice splits batches on descriptor set
  changes via Batch.DescriptorSet/SetTextureSet, and drains pending
  commands before clearing a full set cache.
- Scene.frag compiles both ways under BINDLESS_TEXTURES; without it the
  four samplers are bound directly. EndFlash binds a dummy set since
  nothing is sampled there.
- The scene pipeline layout takes whichever set layout the device can do.

Texture format support (automatic, no env var):

- TextureUploader::GetUploader now takes the physical device and checks
  VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_SAMPLED_IMAGE_BIT plus
  VK_FORMAT_FEATURE_SAMPLED_IMAGE_FILTER_LINEAR_BIT. A format the GPU
  cannot sample or cannot linearly filter (both undefined behavior with
  the engine's samplers) falls back to a CPU decoder writing a format
  the device does support.
- New decoders: BC1/BC2/BC3 -> RGBA8, BC4 -> R8, BC5 -> RG8, RGB8 ->
  RGBA8, RGBA32F -> RGBA8. Without a decoder the upload path uses its
  existing white fallback.
- On the GE8300 every BCn format is unsupported and RGBA32F (lightmaps,
  fog maps) samples but cannot be filtered; without this both produced
  heavy speckle.

Verified on device: intro renders clean (textures, lightmaps, fog); the
PowerVR also needs MSAA disabled via Settings.json (Antialias: Off) --
with 4x MSAA its resolve produces edge speckle -- which the port's
packaging now seeds. Host AMD still selects the bindless path.
